rgery, closely mimicking cancer", "must_not_miss": false, "discriminators": {"history": ["Recent breast trauma, surgery, or biopsy", "May be painless"], "exam": ["Firm, irregular mass that may be fixed; skin dimpling possible", "No axillary lymphadenopathy"], "imaging": ["Coarse, rim-like or 'oil cyst' calcifications on mammography", "Ultrasound shows an irregular hypoechoic area; biopsy may be needed if imaging is indeterminate"]}}, {"name": "Lymphoma involving the breast", "slug": "breast-lymphoma", "why_considered": "Rare but can present as a breast mass, often with systemic B symptoms", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Breast mass with fever, drenching night sweats, or weight loss", "discriminators": {"history": ["B symptoms: fever, night sweats, unintentional weight loss", "May have other nodal disease"], "exam": ["Firm, sometimes bilateral breast masses", "Generalized lymphadenopathy or splenomegaly"], "labs": ["Cytopenias or elevated LDH"], "imaging": ["PET/CT shows hypermetabolic breast and nodal disease; biopsy shows lymphoid cells, not carcinoma"]}}, {"name": "Metastatic disease to the breast from another primary", "slug": "breast-metastasis", "why_considered": "Rare; another cancer (for example, melanoma, lung, or ovarian) can metastasize to the breast and mimic a primary breast tumor", "must_not_miss": true, "trigger": "Known non-breast malignancy with a new breast mass, or bilateral breast masses", "discriminators": {"history": ["Known primary cancer elsewhere", "Bilateral or multiple breast masses"], "exam": ["Breast mass without typical primary breast cancer skin changes", "Signs of the primary tumor elsewhere"], "imaging": ["Imaging features may be atypical; biopsy with immunohistochemistry confirms the origin"]}}], "course": {"severity": {"mild": "Early-stage disease (stage I–IIA): small tumor, no or minimal nodal involvement, no distant spread; patient feels well with a palpable lump or abnormal screening mammogram", "moderate": "Locally advanced